# build output
bin/
obj/
publish/

# user/IDE
*.user
.vs/
.idea/

# probe output
tools/SensorProbe/probe-elevated.txt

# release binaries — these belong on a GitHub Release, not in the tree
installer/Output/

# Screenshots are work-in-progress captures, not release material, and they routinely
# catch other windows. Ignored anywhere in the tree, not just the root — a screenshot
# dropped in docs/ or assets/ would otherwise sail straight into a public repo.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.bmp
*.webp
*.mp4
# real source assets under Assets/ stay tracked (.ico was never matched above)
!src/PwrMon/Assets/*.png
# curated captures for the public landing page. Deliberately narrow: only images placed
# in docs/assets/ escape the blanket ignore above, so an incidental screenshot dropped
# anywhere else still can't reach a public repo. Check every file here for other windows,
# filenames and personal data before committing — these are published.
!docs/assets/*.png
!docs/assets/*.gif

# internal working notes — not for publication
HANDOFF.md
GO-PUBLIC.md
# Branding exploration. The images beside it are already covered by the blanket *.jpg rule,
# so committing the catalogue alone would publish a page of broken image links.
docs/branding/

# Signing key material. The release key lives at ~/.pwrmon/release-key.txt, outside the repo
# entirely, and tools/new-release-key.ps1 defaults it there — this is the backstop for the day
# someone points -OutFile somewhere convenient. A leaked private key hands every installed
# copy of PwrMon an elevated binary of the holder's choosing.
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.snk
release-key*.txt
